# Age of Mortals — weapons, war paint and magic items.
Belaying Pin	PROFICIENCY:WEAPON|Club	TYPE:Weapon.Melee.Simple.Standard.Bludgeoning	COST:1	WT:1	DAMAGE:1d4	CRITMULT:x2	WIELD:Light	SIZE:M	SPROP:A ship's belaying pin used as a club. Simple light melee weapon; 1d3 (Small), 1d4 (Medium); x2; bludgeoning. Price 1 stl. Weapon proficiency: as the book gives no group, proficiency with clubs is used here.	SOURCEPAGE:p.26
Cutlass (Age of Mortals)	PROFICIENCY:WEAPON|Cutlass	TYPE:Weapon.Melee.Martial.Standard.Slashing.Piercing.Sword	COST:15	WT:3	DAMAGE:1d6	CRITRANGE:3	CRITMULT:x2	WIELD:Light	SIZE:M	SPROP:Age of Mortals' cutlass: 15 stl, 18-20/x2 (Legends of the Twins p.16 reprints it at 12 gp, 19-20). Light; slashing and piercing; +2 circumstance bonus to resist being disarmed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.26
Tarmak War Paint	TYPE:Magic.Potion	COST:500	WT:0	SPROP:Magical blue body paint known only to the Tarmak: a creature painted with it gains a +5 natural armor bonus and fast healing 5 until it has healed 20 points in all, when the paint loses its power. Making one application is a DC 25 Craft (alchemy) check. Market price 500 stl.	SOURCEPAGE:p.11
Lost Star	PROFICIENCY:WEAPON|Bastard Sword	TYPE:Magic.Enhancement.Weapon.Melee.Exotic.Specific.Slashing.Sword	COST:0	WT:10	DAMAGE:1d10	CRITRANGE:2	CRITMULT:x2	WIELD:OneHanded	SIZE:M	BONUS:WEAPON|DAMAGE,TOHIT|5|TYPE=Enhancement	SPROP:Qualinesti treasure: a +5 dragon bane mighty cleaving bastard sword with a star sapphire in its pommel. Grants its wielder Exotic Weapon Proficiency (bastard sword) and Cleave. Held overhead in sunlight, evil creatures within 300 feet who see the gem make a Will save (DC 21 + wielder's Charisma modifier) or are fascinated (as the bard's fascination) while the wielder spends a full-round action each round; lowering the sword ends it. Strong conjuration and enchantment; CL 18th. No price is printed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.77
Abyssal Lance (Lesser)	PROFICIENCY:WEAPON|Lance	TYPE:Magic.Enhancement.Weapon.Melee.Martial.Specific.Piercing.Lance.Reach	COST:15210	WT:10	DAMAGE:1d8	CRITMULT:x3	WIELD:TwoHanded	REACHMULT:2	SIZE:M	BONUS:WEAPON|DAMAGE,TOHIT|1|TYPE=Enhancement	SPROP:A darklance: a +1 dragon bane lance against good dragons, emitting light-absorbing dark radiance; it bypasses dragons' damage reduction as an epic weapon. Hardness 17, 40 hit points. Its +1 is superseded by the dragonsteel's natural enhancement bonus. About 10 feet long. Strong conjuration; CL 8th; divine instruction. Market price equivalent 15,210 stl.	SOURCEPAGE:p.78
Abyssal Lance (Greater)	PROFICIENCY:WEAPON|Lance	TYPE:Magic.Enhancement.Weapon.Melee.Martial.Specific.Piercing.Lance.Reach	COST:105210	WT:10	DAMAGE:1d8	CRITMULT:x3	WIELD:TwoHanded	REACHMULT:2	SIZE:M	BONUS:WEAPON|DAMAGE,TOHIT|3|TYPE=Enhancement	SPROP:A +3 unholy dragon bane lance against good dragons; it bypasses dragons' damage reduction as an epic weapon. Hardness 23, 70 hit points. Each hit on a good dragon also deals 1 point of permanent Constitution drain; a critical hit on one drains Constitution equal to the wielder's character level. A good creature wielding it gains two negative levels (never real level loss, removed only by letting it go). Strong conjuration; CL 20th; divine instruction. Market price equivalent 105,210 stl.	SOURCEPAGE:p.78
Glaive of Grimwulf	PROFICIENCY:WEAPON|Glaive	TYPE:Magic.Enhancement.Weapon.Melee.Martial.Specific.Slashing.Polearm.Reach	COST:0	WT:7	DAMAGE:1d10	CRITMULT:x3	WIELD:TwoHanded	REACHMULT:2	SIZE:M	BONUS:WEAPON|DAMAGE,TOHIT|3|TYPE=Enhancement	SPROP:A +3 holy mighty cleaving vorpal glaive of silver-blue adamantine (anarchic instead of holy since Nura Bint-Drax altered it). It ignores hardness of less than 20 when sundering or striking objects, and glows a pale blue that gives no useful light. Moderate evocation, strong necromancy and transmutation; CL 18th. No price is printed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.78-79
Sword of Tears	PROFICIENCY:WEAPON|Longsword	TYPE:Magic.Enhancement.Weapon.Melee.Martial.Specific.Slashing.Sword.Intelligent	COST:109315	WT:4	DAMAGE:1d8	CRITRANGE:2	CRITMULT:x2	WIELD:OneHanded	SIZE:M	BONUS:WEAPON|DAMAGE,TOHIT|5|TYPE=Enhancement	SPROP:A +5 keen sword of life stealing, made by Sargonnas. Intelligent and evil (Int 14, Wis 12, Cha 12, Ego 15); it tries to control a non-evil wielder. Its wielder may use Combat Reflexes and Improved Sunder as often as desired. It cannot feed on creatures of the Chaos subtype. Strong necromancy and moderate transmutation; CL 17th; Craft Magic Arms and Armor, keen edge, energy drain, creator must be evil. Price 109,315 stl. (Weight not printed; a longsword's.)	SOURCEPAGE:p.80
Mina's Kiss	PROFICIENCY:WEAPON|Mace (Heavy)	TYPE:Magic.Enhancement.Weapon.Melee.Simple.Specific.Bludgeoning.Mace.Artifact	COST:0	WT:10	DAMAGE:1d8	CRITMULT:x2	WIELD:OneHanded	SIZE:M	BONUS:WEAPON|DAMAGE,TOHIT|5|TYPE=Enhancement	SPROP:Artifact: a +5 ghost touch unholy heavy mace of wounding of solid gold. While held: constant deathwatch and the protection of death ward. Kiss of death: a blow that brings a victim to -1 hit points or lower casts death knell and animate dead; the victim makes a Will save (DC 20) or dies and rises as a zombie under the wielder's control, and the wielder heals 1d8 (not above maximum), gains +2 profane to Strength and +1 effective caster level for 10 minutes per HD of the slain (at most +10 Strength and +5 caster level at once). Strong necromancy; CL 20th.	SOURCEPAGE:p.80
Collar of Hounds	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous.Neck	COST:45000	WT:1	SPROP:On a canine, with its command word, the dog obeys whoever activated it, seeing them as friendly (responding only to commands it knows). On a humanoid, refusing a one-word command from the one who placed it deals 1d4 electricity damage; a Will save (DC 17) when first placed prevents attunement, and only the one who placed it can remove it. Faint enchantment and evocation; CL 5th; Craft Wondrous Item, charm animal, shocking grasp, suggestion. Market price equivalent 45,000 stl.	SOURCEPAGE:p.79
Road Block	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:6050	WT:0	SPROP:A 20-foot woven rope. Laid roughly straight on the ground with its command word spoken, it becomes a permanent, non-magical wall of stone 10 feet tall, 20 feet long and 5 feet thick; for its first 5 minutes no spell of 4th level or lower works within 10 feet of it. Moderate conjuration and abjuration; CL 11th; Craft Wondrous Item, globe of invulnerability, wall of stone. Price 6,050 stl.	SOURCEPAGE:p.79
Helm of the Titans	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous.Headgear	COST:116000	WT:0	SPROP:A bronze helm sized for an ogre (Large). Once attuned by its command word: +4 competence on Charisma checks and Charisma-based skill checks with ogres, +2 with goblinoids, -4 with anyone else; the wearer understands, speaks and reads Ogre. A non-ogre wearer gains a +2 deflection bonus to AC and darkvision 60 feet. An ogre wearer gains those, and instead of the language, detect thoughts on any ogre within 5 miles with telepathic replies, and can command up to 100 attuned ogres whose names he knows as suggestion with no save (ogre-subtype creatures that are not true ogres, such as half-ogres, ogre magi and minotaurs, save at DC 15; ogre titans are immune). Moderate divination and enchantment; CL 12th; Craft Wondrous Item, detect thoughts, shield, suggestion, tongues, creator must be an ogre. Price 116,000 stl.	SOURCEPAGE:p.79-80
Robe of Shadows	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous.Robe	COST:54880	WT:1	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|3|TYPE=Armor	BONUS:SAVE|ALL|2|TYPE=Resistance	BONUS:MISC|SR|15	SPROP:Ebony cloth: +3 armor bonus to AC, spell resistance 15, a +2 resistance bonus on all saves, and once a day a shadowy gaseous form as cast by an 11th-level sorcerer. Strong varied; CL 11th; Craft Wondrous Item, antimagic field, gaseous form, mage armor or shield of faith. Price 54,880 stl.	SOURCEPAGE:p.123
Censer of Eternal Flame	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous	COST:12500	WT:1	SPROP:Filled with clear water, it raises a 3-foot pillar of blue and crimson flame that gives bright light but no heat and burns nothing, for as long as the water stays. Made by the priests of Sirrion. Faint evocation; CL 3rd; Craft Wondrous Item, continual flame. Price 12,500 gp; XP 500.	SOURCEPAGE:p.151
Flames of the Storm	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous.Artifact	COST:0	WT:25	SPROP:Zeboim's unique crystal ball, a black sea opal on a silver sea-serpent stand. In use it flickers with seafire, and the scried subject is outlined as by faerie fire. Three times a day, control winds through it, or once a day control weather (only to make the weather worse). Moderate divination, strong transmutation; CL 18th. No price is printed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.166
Medallion of the One God	TYPE:Magic.Wondrous.Neck.Artifact	COST:0	WT:0	SPROP:Dragonsteel, given to Mina by Takhisis. Acts as a medallion of faith, and: a cleric of the One God gains +5 effective spellcaster levels (spells per day and caster level, nothing else); +6 profane bonus on Charisma-based skill checks with evil individuals, +4 with neutral, +2 with good (also when rebuking or controlling undead); constant death ward and see invisibility. No price is printed.	SOURCEPAGE:p.198
Device of Time Journeying (Age of Mortals)	TYPE:Artifact.Major	SPROP:As printed in Age of Mortals: a jeweled scepter folding into a pendant, activated by its chant; it carries everyone within 10 feet, always including its user, through time and space, arriving at the desired time or place, rarely both, without a DC 20 Use Magic Device check (+1 per 100 years back, +2 per decade forward). Antipathy (30th-level sorcerer) against thieves; lost or given away, it returns to the last person to activate it. Usable only by the First Races (elves, humans, ogres); one of the Graygem races using it lets Chaos alter the time stream. If broken, a DC 25 Craft (tinkering) check repairs it. Legends of the Twins (pp.29-30) reprints it.	SOURCEPAGE:p.80-81
